  "name": "2.0 L turbo four, direct injection",
  "notes": "The 2.0 L EA888 generation 3 of the Mk7 Golf GTI: 82.5 x 92.8 mm (1984 cc), 9.6:1, direct and port injection, both cams phased, two-stage exhaust valve lift, one IHI IS20 turbo with an electric wastegate (Audi SSP 920243; the turbo's model: eqtuning.com, enthusiast); 162 kW at 4500 to 6200 rpm, 350 N m from 1500 to 4400 (VW's press presentation). What is known and what is guessed: the exhaust's two lobes are gen 2's (SSP 922903: the small 6.35 mm, 180 deg, used to about 3100 rpm and from just after a start above -10 C; the large 10 mm, 215 deg; durations read at 1 mm); the intake phaser's 60 deg is the earlier 2.0 TSI's; the exhaust phaser's 42 deg is the EA855 2.5 TFSI's (SSP 920273: gen 3's own and its parked timing not published); the boost taper (1.2 bar to 4500 rpm, 0.7 by 7000) is judgement, its top end agreeing with an owner's stock log (81 kPa at 6048 rpm: carworklog.com); the turbo's wheels are the IS20's as rebuilders and a blog give them (compressor 42.5 / 54.0 mm, turbine about 50 mm, about 1 mm either way; no maker's figure), its A/Rs matched (none found). Front drive, six-speed dual clutch. Its exhaust: a cast or short log manifold, the primaries 0.61 times the layout's length: the class the real engine carries (recalled), its length JUDGEMENT. Its cams' second duration: the seat-to-1 mm step 19 deg a side, the finger class's rule, the 1 mm duration held and the seat moved (section 8 of the judgement sources). Its knock-limit table is baked (the degrees taken from the best-torque spark by speed and load, baked in the app's own order: cams.py). Its intake cam map is baked (the cam swept at full load, the best advance by speed: cams.py).",
